cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ArchAnchor, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: ArchAnchor
abstract: >-
  ArchAnchor reads a Java codebase and recovers its architectural constraints, the rules about
  which module may depend on which package, by electing a reference class per module: the class
  whose dependencies best represent what the module was meant to be. It reports the dependencies
  that step outside those constraints as violations, recommends splits, merges and moves that
  remove them, and exports the constraints.
